    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0941" n="931" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg931"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/12–1647</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Assistant Secretary of the Air Force</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitney</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-16">December 16,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Whitney</hi>: You will recall that at
                    the Committee of Two meeting on November 3, 1947, at which you were present,
                    certain decisions were reached with regard to assisting the Chinese Government
                    in the acquisition of military supplies; it was agreed, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >inter alia</hi> (page 1, paragraph 1, sub-paragraph <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >c</hi> of the minutes), to “expedite deliveries of equipment to complete
                    the 8⅓ Group Program.”</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has authorized this Department to inform the Department of
                    the Air Force that, as the London meeting of the Council of Foreign Ministers
                    has terminated, the decisions reached at the Committee of Two meeting referred
                    to above can be put into effect forthwith. The Foreign Liquidation Commissioner
                    is also being advised in the above sense. Would you be so kind as to ensure <pb
                        facs="0942" n="932" xml:id="pg932"/> that the concerned officials of the
                    Department of the Air Force are also apprised of this information.</p>
                <p>A similar communication is being sent to the Department of the Army<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d729-f1"/> with respect to the decision of the Committee of Two
                    referred to in sub-paragraph paragraph 1, page 1 of the minutes of the meeting
                    on November 3, 1947.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton Butterworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
